{
  "requirement": "`AgentSettings<D>` identifies the configurations a domain can use in its cache.\nTBV implements this sealed trait for `AgentConfig` and `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait AgentSettings<D: Domain>: Settings<D> { }\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement says `AgentSettings<D>` identifies the configurations a domain can use in its cache. It also says TBV implements this sealed trait for `AgentConfig` and `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n\nI derived three obligations and mapped each to a test:\n\n1. **Sealed.** Third parties must not be able to implement the trait. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#trait[AgentSettings]` has a `compile_fail` doctest. The doctest tries `impl<D: Domain> AgentSettings<D> for ThirdPartyConfig {}`. The trait has the private supertrait `sealed::Settings<D>`, so the doctest fails to compile for the intended reason. A `compile_fail` doctest is a loose check, since it would also pass on an unrelated error. I did not treat that as a gap.\n2. **Implemented for `AgentConfig`.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` passes an `AgentConfig::Bedrock` to `ValidationCache::with_agent`. That function takes `impl AgentSettings<D>`, so the test compiles only if `AgentConfig` implements the trait. The test then asserts the cache uses the configuration.\n3. **Implemented for `AgentWithTools<D>`.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[registered_tools_use_the_current_context_and_ordinary_node_ids]` passes `backend.with_tool(...)`, which is an `AgentWithTools`, to `with_agent`. It also exercises the configuration at runtime. It checks the tool list sent to the agent and the tool usage stats.\n\nBoth tests and the trait item carry `{test}` references to the requirement, so there is no marking gap. The trait has no behavior of its own, so the sealing check and the two impls are the whole requirement. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "cec8dc27c3b2606c94129fd6e5a30835b88f6c749b7486e187768c03410c8bbd",
